
digdir — first-run setup (host half)
====================================

  Generating secrets that can be generated:
      CONFIG_MASTER_KEY  generated
      JWT_SECRET  generated
      TYPESENSE_API_KEY_ADMIN  generated

  Values that cannot be invented:
      AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY  SKIPPED — still needs a value before the LLM path works
      AZURE_OPENAI_API_ENDPOINT  SKIPPED — still needs a value before the LLM path works
      AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT_NAME  SKIPPED — still needs a value before the LLM path works

  Optional services — blank is a fine answer:
      COLBERT_API_URL  skipped — reranking stays off. Answers keep retrieval
                            order: slightly worse ORDERING, not fewer
                            or wrong answers.
      COLBERT_API_KEY  skipped — reranking stays off. Answers keep retrieval
                            order: slightly worse ORDERING, not fewer
                            or wrong answers.

  Which LLM provider should this instance use?
    true  = Azure OpenAI, using the three values above.
    false = any OpenAI-compatible server, including a local one.
      AZURE_OPENAI_USE_AZURE  already set, left alone

  Who may administer this instance:
      ADMIN_USER_EMAILS  SKIPPED — no admin will exist and every login will be refused

  3 generated, 0 left alone.

  ⚠ Still placeholder or empty: AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY AZURE_OPENAI_API_ENDPOINT AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT_NAME
    The server will refuse to start until these are real values.

  ⚠ Still unset: ADMIN_USER_EMAILS
    The stack will start and refuse every login, with nothing saying why.
    Set it in .env (uncommented) and re-run the database half.

  Next: seed the database, BEFORE starting the server —

      docker compose -f docker-compose.newcomer.yml run --rm digdir-rag \
        java -cp /app/app.jar clojure.main -m digdir.setup.bootstrap

  Then create the admin account named above. Seeding does NOT create it:

      docker compose -f docker-compose.newcomer.yml run --rm digdir-rag \
        java -cp /app/app.jar clojure.main -m digdir.setup.first-admin

  Only now start the server. There is NO restart step:

      docker compose -f docker-compose.newcomer.yml up -d

  Seeded with nothing running, the account persists and login works on the
  FIRST attempt. Seeded against a running server it silently does not, and
  restarting afterwards does not recover it. docs/onboarding.md carries the
  measurements (#526, #537, #538).

